  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Lissajous figures and the function generator"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "With the time base off, one signal goes to the X plates and another to the Y plates. The pattern is a Lissajous figure. Its shape gives the frequency ratio: $f_y/f_x$ = (number of points touching a horizontal tangent)/(number touching a vertical tangent). For equal frequencies the figure shows the phase: a line for 0° or 180°, an ellipse in between with $\\sin\\phi$ = (Y-intercept)/(maximum Y), and a circle for 90° with equal amplitudes. A function generator supplies sine, square and triangular waves whose frequency and amplitude can be set, for testing circuits."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "f_y/f_x = horizontal tangencies / vertical tangencies"
    },
    {
     "en": "sin φ = Y-intercept / Y-maximum"
    },
    {
     "en": "Function generator: sine, square, triangle"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A Lissajous figure compares two signals. The ratio of horizontal to vertical tangent points gives f y over f x, and the shape of an ellipse gives the phase difference.",
    "kn": "ಲಿಸಾಜೂ ಆಕೃತಿ ಎರಡು ಸಂಕೇತಗಳನ್ನು ಹೋಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಅಡ್ಡ ಮತ್ತು ಲಂಬ ಸ್ಪರ್ಶಕ ಬಿಂದುಗಳ ಅನುಪಾತ fy/fx ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ; ದೀರ್ಘವೃತ್ತದ ಆಕಾರ ಹಂತ ವ್ಯತ್ಯಾಸ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
